<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-010-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) regeneration as a lawful growth process — Durbin/Ellis tadpole tail curves — MorphoEval overall 78.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 remediated assessment. All Pass 1 remediation items are closed: a decay-exponent sweep shows the integrated power law is best at n = 1.2 (free fit 1.15) and 5x worse at Thompson's n = 2; an amputation-level sweep through the Fig. 40 law shows the pure cubic parabola already fits the four series (RMSE 0.11 d) and that the 75 % divergence is not demanded by data below 57 % (free gamma = 0.00); exact permutation tests give p = 1/24 for both the day-9 and plateau amount-removed correlations; R-independent and constant-velocity nulls are 4.8x / 19x / 13.5x worse than the fitted laws; KS p = 0.47 / 0.92 on residuals; the vendored L. clamitans specimen is segmented (tail fraction 0.655 vs Thompson's 0.65 / 0.62) and overlaid; every exported measurement that has a literature value carries reference_value; the Dryad digest is pinned on LF bytes so verify_sha256 passes from a clone; GIF clipping and the Exp. IV axis floor are fixed. Verdict: supported, with two documented caveats against Thompson's own glosses (V t^2 exponent; extrapolated 75 % asymptote). Overall 78.9/100 (faithfulness 76.9, reproducibility 83.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 6f3b0adec; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 68, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_010_the_rate_of_growth_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-010_the-rate-of-growth.py at 6f3b0adec, image/png, 734418 B, 1950×1755 px, artifact_sha256 cd24ca6582e91fdb9168ab585566a46ee223a016ec636a9c1b8c052a554ad2a0 (sha256 cd24ca6582e91fdb9168ab585566a46ee223a016ec636a9c1b8c052a554ad2a0), spec_fingerprint bffecc9effec0ed61f93d27b11061055edc430bd0988d9f85d96335fb77a665c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: bffecc9effec0ed61f93d27b11061055edc430bd0988d9f85d96335fb77a665c; artifact_sha256: cd24ca6582e91fdb9168ab585566a46ee223a016ec636a9c1b8c052a554ad2a0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-010/lithobates_clamitans_tadpole_specimen.jpg=4a90d205c4f3ec5e..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-010/t1917_010_the_rate_of_growth_reference.json=afba32ab058719d6..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-010/thompson_p139_durbin_expII_regeneration.csv=ee7b4283ace77101..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-010/thompson_p141_durbin_expII_interpolated.csv=b44610d153e0e230..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-010/thompson_p144_durbin_expIV_regeneration.csv=cc4848894d2310d1..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-010/thompson_p148_ellis_tail_regeneration.csv=3b61cc051e28ff22..., morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_010.lean=36af9a4ae4b3f5de...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-010-the-rate-of-growth-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 139-145 reproduces Durbin's Exp. II and Exp. IV regenerated-length tables and asserts V falls 'inversely as the square of the time' with log V approximately linear (Fig. 37) and an inflection 'about the seventh day' in Exp. IV | Thompson (1917) p. 148 reproduces Ellis's series O/P/R/S (12-57 % of tail removed) and constructs Fig. 40 isochrones that 'approximate in form to a cubic parabola' and 'converge towards infinity' at 75 % removed (Ellis's lethal fifth series) | Thompson (1917) p. 148: tail length 'very near to 26 mm., or 65 per cent. of the whole body-length'; reconstructed_in_script: Least-squares fits of exponential-approach, hyperbolic, generalised power-decay (free n), logistic and Gompertz laws; OLS decay exponents; sweeps over n and over amputation level R through t_q = a R^(1/3) (75/(75-R))^gamma; exact 4! permutation tests; constant-velocity and R-independent nulls; KS tests on standardised residuals | Computer-vision tail fraction on one CC-BY lateral photograph (threshold, principal axis, width profile, terminal monotone-taper criterion); transfer_boundary: No transfer to a modern regeneration time series: Dryad doi:10.5061/dryad.n6n6495 (skink telomeres, single endpoint, YES/NO amputation) is a DATASET_MISMATCH, vendored for provenance only and excluded from the verdict; does_not_claim: A mechanistic model of tail regeneration; that the exponential/Gompertz laws are the generative process rather than descriptive fits to 7-10 printed points per series; or that one photograph establishes the population tail proportion." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add a second CC-licensed specimen (ideally a regenerating tadpole tail) to move specimen-match beyond a single photograph",
        "remediation needed: Digitise Ellis's per-individual data from the J. Exp. Zool. scan to raise n beyond the four printed series means",
        "remediation needed: Record the installed wheel versions in result.json for a byte-level environment pin" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.89e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

